    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aCrxZh1CjrgI"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Interpretation — Section 1\n",
        "\n",
        "- Mean body mass ≈ 4207 g, SD ≈ 805 g — dispersion is substantial relative to the mean.\n",
        "- Skewness ≈ +0.47: a mild right tail, not a serious departure from symmetry.\n",
        "- Excess kurtosis ≈ −0.74: platykurtic — flatter than normal, thinner tails.\n",
        "- The overall density is bimodal, and the species curves explain why: Gentoo penguins are much heavier than Adélie and Chinstrap. The pooled distribution is a mixture of species, so pooled summary statistics are misleading on their own — which motivates the grouped analysis in Sections 3–5.\n",
        "- Adélie and Chinstrap overlap almost entirely in mass; Gentoo separates cleanly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BweJHerAjrgI"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Hypothesis Testing — do male and female penguins differ in mean body mass?\n",
        "\n",
        "- $H_0: \\mu_{\\text{male}} = \\mu_{\\text{female}}$\n",
        "- $H_1: \\mu_{\\text{male}} \\neq \\mu_{\\text{female}}$ (two-tailed)\n",
        "\n",
        "Significance level $\\alpha = 0.05$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "oq8sVbwMjrgI",
        "outputId": "b602b47b-3238-43e7-c7a3-9ec118798637"
      },
      "source": [
        "# ---- Normality within each sex ------------------------------------------\n",
        "mass_f <- peng$body_mass_g[peng$sex == \"female\"]\n",
        "mass_m <- peng$body_mass_g[peng$sex == \"male\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "cat(\"n(female) =\", length(mass_f), \" n(male) =\", length(mass_m), \"\\n\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "cat(\"--- Shapiro-Wilk: female ---\\n\")\n",
        "print(shapiro.test(mass_f))\n",
        "\n",
        "cat(\"--- Shapiro-Wilk: male ---\\n\")\n",
        "print(shapiro.test(mass_m))"
      ],
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "n(female) = 165  n(male) = 168 \n",
            "\n",
            "--- Shapiro-Wilk: female ---\n",
            "\n",
            "\tShapiro-Wilk normality test\n",
            "\n",
            "data:  mass_f\n",
            "W = 0.91931, p-value = 6.155e-08\n",
            "\n",
            "--- Shapiro-Wilk: male ---\n",
            "\n",
            "\tShapiro-Wilk normality test\n",
            "\n",
            "data:  mass_m\n",
            "W = 0.92504, p-value = 1.227e-07\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 617
        },
        "id": "EKgQfeCnjrgI",
        "outputId": "7e4b7190-d52a-4d5f-badb-dddf1765da66"
      },
      "source": [
        "# ---- QQ-plots by sex ----------------------------------------------------\n",
        "par(mfrow = c(1, 2))\n",
        "\n",
        "qqnorm(mass_f, main = \"QQ-Plot: Female Body Mass\")\n",
        "qqline(mass_f, col = \"red\", lwd = 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "qqnorm(mass_m, main = \"QQ-Plot: Male Body Mass\")\n",
        "qqline(mass_m, col = \"red\", lwd = 2)\n",
        "\n",
        "par(mfrow = c(1, 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "if (HAS_GG) {\n",
        "  print(ggplot(peng, aes(sample = body_mass_g)) +\n",
        "          stat_qq() +\n",
        "          stat_qq_line(colour = \"red\") +\n",
        "          facet_wrap(~ sex) +\n",
        "          labs(title = \"Normal QQ-Plots of Body Mass by Sex\",\n",
        "               x = \"Theoretical quantiles\", y = \"Sample quantiles\") +\n",
        "          theme_minimal(base_size = 13))\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
